\": \"The Meridian API shall persist customer orders and dispatch allocations using the serving warehouse's deployment-configured cut-off, working-day, holiday, time-zone, and customer shelf-life rules, and enforce idempotency, order validation, pre-packing customer changes, and cancellation rules.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"ASM-6\",\n    \"ASM-11\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Released stock is available for an order from its serving warehouse and has eligible lots.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record shows earliest-expiry eligible lots first, applies minimum remaining shelf life, uses greater stability-budget usage first for tied expiry dates, and exposes each allocation and outstanding quantity.\",\n     \"when\": \"The order is allocated.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Suitable stock is insufficient for a partial order or any line of a complete-only order.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The partial order response shows allocated and outstanding quantities without over-allocating stock, while the complete-only order holds no stock until every line can be fully allocated.\",\n     \"when\": \"Allocation is attempted.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Multiple orders are submitted concurrently against the same available handling units.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response records and stock list show no unit allocated to more than one order and total allocated quantity does not exceed physical available quantity.\",\n     \"when\": \"The allocations are committed.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits an allocation override with a reason, without a reason, or to stock violating Released status or customer shelf life.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The valid response record includes the reason and changed allocation, while each invalid response status is 400 or 409 and the original allocation remains unchanged.\",\n     \"when\": \"The override operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Suitable stock is released for waiting back orders.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The order response records show oldest-first back-order allocation.\",\n     \"when\": \"The allocation service updates affected orders.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An older back order awaits suitable stock or a complete-only order cannot be fully allocated.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.6\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record shows eligible back orders filled in submission order and no stock held by the incomplete complete-only order.\",\n     \"when\": \"Suitable stock is released or allocation is attempted.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall allocate only released, physically available stock meeting customer minimum remaining shelf life, select earliest expiry first with the specified stability-budget tie-break, and apply complete-order, partial-order, back-order, and override rules.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator submits a pack request for allocated stock.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the box, logger, lot quantities, operator, and seal time; a reused logger or incompatible packing response status is 409.\",\n     \"when\": \"The requested box contains one logger, products with the same storage band, and a compatible box type.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits a route with date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the requested route values and a conflicting driver or vehicle assignment returns status 409.\",\n     \"when\": \"The route is created, updated, or confirmed.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A route's packed box would exceed qualified duration less the configured safety margin at a planned arrival.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 409 and the response message identifies the box and qualification shortfall or duration overrun.\",\n     \"when\": \"The route confirmation operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A driver calls route listing, route detail, scan, departure, or synchronization operations for the authenticated driver's route.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list or record contains only that driver's authorized route, ordered stops, expected boxes, scans, and departure state.\",\n     \"when\": \"The driver supplies contracted date, action identifiers, or route data.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A driver synchronizes queued actions with distinct action identifiers or repeats an action identifier.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains accepted and conflicting actions, and the resulting route history contains each accepted action only once.\",\n     \"when\": \"The synchronization operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A driver submits a handover with receiver, acknowledgement, signature, photo, completion time, and box delivery or refusal quantities.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.6\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record and delivery-evidence response contain persisted evidence and quantities, and refused quantities retain the refusal reason.\",\n     \"when\": \"The handover operation is called and authorized delivery evidence is subsequently fetched.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A confirmed route is changed before its driver has left for the affected stop.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.7\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the changed schedule or stop order and an email call or driver-change event is recorded.\",\n     \"when\": \"A dispatcher updates the route schedule or stop order.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist compatible box packing and route plans, enforce box and route qualification, and record driver loading, departure, synchronization, handover, refusal, and delivery-evidence operations.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"ASM-3\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall process readings from contracted receipt logger uploads and from the configured authenticated logger gateway through the locked contract operation, expose temperature histories for contracted entity types, and persist available readings, gaps, excursions, tier-by-tier handling-unit budgets, related holds, and corrected history when readings arrive late or out of order.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"ASM-10\",\n    \"Q-10\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A contracted receipt logger upload contains repeated, late, out-of-order, future-dated, or pre-sealing readings.\",\n     \"when\": \"The file is processed and temperature history is requested for its entity and date range.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record places readings at their occurred times, stores a duplicate once, flags future and pre-sealing readings as excluded from calculations, and shows unavailable-reading gaps.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"given\": \"Three consecutive in-band readings follow an out-of-band reading in persisted history.\",\n     \"when\": \"The related temperature history and handling-unit record are requested.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response records show the excursion open from the first out-of-band reading until the third consecutive in-band reading and show time charged to each applicable tier.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A handling unit has excursion history or a late reading changes that history.\",\n     \"when\": \"The handling-unit or temperature-history operation is called after recalculation.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record shows separate budgets for portions with different histories, updated remaining tier allowances, excursion links, holds, and an audit event for the correction.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.4\",\n     \"given\": \"An excursion begins, a tier allowance falls below 25 percent, a tier is exhausted, or a not-permitted range is reached.\",\n     \"when\": \"The triggering reading is received and processed.\",\n     \"then\": \"An email call is recorded within 120 seconds for the required driver when on-route, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers, and affected stock response records have On Hold status pending a decision.\",\n     \"level\": \"job\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.5\",\n     \"given\": \"A logger has sent no reading for 15 minutes and its box is out for delivery.\",\n     \"when\": \"The silent-device check runs and temperature history is requested.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record marks the device silent, shows the gap, and an alert email call is recorded.\",\n     \"level\": \"job\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.6\",\n     \"given\": \"A cold room or its temperature records are available.\",\n     \"when\": \"A caller lists cold rooms, retrieves a cold room, or requests temperature history for a room, box, lot, handling unit, or device.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list or record contains the latest reading, status, gaps, alerts, history timestamps, and applicable band and excursion markers.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.7\",\n     \"given\": \"A handling unit has recorded temperature history with an interval containing no readings and a stored profile band.\",\n     \"when\": \"The caller fetches temperature history for the unit or its box, lot, device, or cold room.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response contains readings in recorded-time order, an explicit gap, and temperature-band and excursion fields for the requested interval.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.8\",\n     \"given\": \"The configured authenticated logger gateway has a batch of readings for known devices, including duplicate, late, or out-of-order readings.\",\n     \"when\": \"The gateway submits the batch through the locked contract operation using its configured credentials.\",\n     \"then\": \"The persisted reading rows contain each valid reading once at its occurred time, and contracted temperature-history responses show the same ordered readings and calculated history regardless of batch arrival order.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.9\",\n     \"given\": \"A logger-gateway batch contains readings for a known device, but the request has missing or invalid gateway credentials.\",\n     \"when\": \"The gateway submits the batch through the locked contract operation.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and a subsequent temperature-history response contains no reading from the batch.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.10\",\n     \"given\": \"A logger-gateway batch contains at least one valid reading for a known device and also contains a reading for an unknown device or malformed reading data.\",\n     \"when\": \"The gateway submits the batch through the locked contract operation using valid credentials.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400 and subsequent temperature-history responses contain none of the readings from the rejected batch.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Officer submits a disposition proposal subject to the two-person approval workflow, with disposition, reason, and identity confirmation.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the proposal and actor, the proposing officer cannot approve their own proposal, and a different eligible manager's approval or return is recorded without replacing the proposal; this approval restriction does not apply to an ordinary receipt release under AC-7.6.\",\n     \"when\": \"The proposal is retrieved or a decision is submitted by the proposing officer or an eligible different Quality Manager.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A quality decision exists for stock that has not been destroyed or delivered, and an authorized caller submits a separately signed superseding decision.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the new current decision and the earlier decision remains in the returned decision history; the stock status reflects the superseding disposition, a change away from Released removes remaining allocations and applies the contracted replacement-allocation rules, and a decision that would change the status of destroyed or delivered quantity returns status 409 with the prior decision and stock status unchanged.\",\n     \"when\": \"The supersede operation is called and the decision and affected stock are subsequently retrieved.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Rejected stock has a positive quantity to destroy.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains those values and the destroyed quantity is removed from available stock.\",\n     \"when\": \"An authorized caller submits a destruction date, quantity, and witness.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A handling unit has tiered budget usage and a related quality case.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response contains the used and remaining value for each tier and linked case telemetry and decision fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"An authorized Quality Officer fetches the unit and quality case.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 7,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/AppDb.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\\n{\\n}\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist quality cases, signed proposals and decisions, superseding decisions, and destruction records, apply the required two-person quality approval, make the latest valid signed disposition authoritative for extant stock, and preserve prior decision history without restoring stock already destroyed or delivered.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An eligible Quality Manager starts a signed recall for selected product lots.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response records identify affected stock, warehouse locations, boxes, routes, deliveries, customer response progress, and recalled held stock is unavailable for allocation.\",\n     \"when\": \"The recall is started and its record and trace are requested.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer submits or updates a recall response for an authorized delivery.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains on-hand, used, destroyed, and stated-disposition values and recall progress reflects the submitted quantities.\",\n     \"when\": \"The recall response operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A recall has unaccounted quantity or all quantity is accounted for.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 409 for closure with unaccounted quantity and no valid write-off, or the response record contains the signed closure or write-off when preconditions are met.\",\n     \"when\": \"A Quality Manager submits closure or a signed write-off.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A started recall has affected warehouse, box, route, and delivery records.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response lists contain the chronological trace of the lot through warehouse, boxes, routes, deliveries, movements, and destruction records.\",\n     \"when\": \"Recall-trace and lot-history operations are called.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist signed recalls, trace selected lots through affected stock and delivery records, block affected stock still held, and record customer responses and signed closure or write-off decisions until quantities are accounted for.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated customer requests orders, deliveries, delivery details, certificates, certificate files, or recall notices.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list, record, or PDF file contains only records belonging to that customer's organisation.\",\n     \"when\": \"The corresponding customer operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator submits a valid saved address or invitation, changes an address, or removes an address or team member within their organisation.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record or action result identifies the change and subsequent lists contain the updated organisation-scoped address or team record.\",\n     \"when\": \"The contracted customer-administration operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator attempts to edit or remove an address or member belonging to another organisation.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 403 or the contract-defined not-found status and no other-organisation row is changed.\",\n     \"when\": \"The contracted customer-administration operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated customer account has a saved language preference.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the saved language value and a value outside the contract enum returns status 400.\",\n     \"when\": \"The account is retrieved and patched with `en` or `ar`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement customer organisation account, address, team, delivery, certificate, recall-notice, order, and language-preference operations with returned records and mutations scoped to the authenticated organisation.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-9\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator requests organisations, organization details, accounts, or account details.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list or record contains persisted organization, member, address, shelf-life, role, and access-assignment values within caller authorization scope.\",\n     \"when\": \"The corresponding list or retrieval operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator creates, updates, or deactivates an account or updates an organization's minimum remaining shelf life.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status and record or action result reflect the new account state, roles, assignments, or minimum shelf-life value.\",\n     \"when\": \"The contracted administration operation is called.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authorized caller requests an operational report for a permitted date range and warehouse or requests lot history.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record or list contains only authorized report values and chronologically ordered receipt, movement, delivery, and destruction events for the requested lot.\",\n     \"when\": \"The report or lot-history operation is called.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement contracted administration, operational-report, and lot-history operations, persisting organisation shelf-life settings, account role and warehouse assignments, and chronological business records.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A consequential contracted change or decision is successfully recorded.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list contains the event's actor, timestamp, action type, affected record, and applies the supplied filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"An authorized caller queries audit events using supported search, date, action-type, or user filters.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An audit event has been recorded.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list still contains the event and a write attempt against the audit event returns status 403.\",\n     \"when\": \"Time passes and the event is queried again or a write is attempted.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated actor performs a consequential contracted mutation or decision.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list and audit row contain the actor, event time, and action type.\",\n     \"when\": \"The operation completes and the authorized audit-events operation is queried for the actor and time range.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall record the actor and timestamp for consequential contracted changes and decisions in read-only audit events and retain those events without automatic expiry.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The database configuration is invalid.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The process exits before serving contracted operations and startup output contains an error.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API process starts.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API is running and its configured database becomes unavailable during a contracted operation.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 500 with the contract-defined `server_error` code and no success response or success record is returned.\",\n     \"when\": \"The operation is called.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall fail startup when persistent-storage configuration is invalid and return the contract-defined server-error response without reporting a business operation as successful when storage is unavailable during a contracted operation.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-8\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"No later than 120 seconds after the triggering reading is received by the operation.\",\n   \"text\": \"Excursion alerts are sent through the configured email channel to the driver when applicable, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers after the triggering reading is received through the contracted authenticated logger-gateway operation.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"metric\": \"5,000 devices reporting at once.\",\n   \"text\": \"The contracted authenticated logger-gateway operation and temperature-data processing capability support concurrent readings from logger and cold-room devices.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of audit rows created by consequential-operation tests have non-empty actor and event-time fields; 0 audit rows are automatically expired.\",\n   \"text\": \"Consequential-operation audit events contain an actor and event time and are retained without automatic expiry.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Portal, customer-portal, staff web, and mobile-application screens or client-side offline storage; this run implements the API side only.\",\n  \"Uncontracted API operations and broader workflows not exposed by contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n  \"Legacy spreadsheet or paper-process data migration.\",\n  \"SMS and push notification delivery, social sign-in, alternate single sign-on, and vendor-specific logger clients.\",\n  \"An additional general inbound logger or temperature-ingestion API not present in the locked contract.\"\n ],\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"ASM-1's email-and-password, one-time-code, and password-reset-link assumption applies only to customer accounts; its exclusion of social sign-in and alternate single sign-on applies only to customers. Staff sign-in remains separate and uses the Meridian Microsoft identity provider required for staff.\",\n  \"Deployment supplies database connection, email sender, Meridian Microsoft identity-provider configuration, and the initial System Administrator identity, warehouse and customer-organisation bootstrap records. No legacy business data is imported. Operational business records are entered through contracted API operations. Explicitly enabling `Seed:Demo` loads deployment-supplied demo rows only for demo/test use.\",\n  \"The configured logger supplier gateway submits telemetry through the locked authenticated contract operation using gateway credentials/configuration supplied for deployment; no additional public HTTP operation or vendor-specific client is added. Email is the only notification channel, using fixed templates; no SMS or push.\",\n  \"Temperature-history and excursion behavior operates on data available through contracted receipt logger uploads, the configured authenticated gateway operation, and persisted contracted records.\",\n  \"Expiry processing is an application-side scheduled check and records dispatcher alerts; test time may be controlled.\",\n  \"Warehouse-specific cut-off times, safety margins, local time zones, working days, and holiday calendars are supplied through deployment-managed warehouse configuration; no configuration API or screen is added.\",\n  \"The existing root health response, generated OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI remain available.\",\n  \"Email and password with an emailed reset link and one-time code are used for customer authentication; no social sign-in or alternate single sign-on is used for customer accounts.\",\n  \"By what channel must the API deliver operational alerts to drivers, dispatchers, and Quality Officers when the requirements say they must be alerted? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\",\n  \"Use each warehouse's configured local time zone and a calendar maintained in warehouse configuration.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nReview the spec."}